From 6eb28f20455a7cdac41901f5ad8a308985ab3d40 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The browser Authors <noreply@browser.invalid>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 17:39:17 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 17/61] video-recording

Browser.startVideoRecording, setVideoRecordingTarget, pauseVideoRecording,
resumeVideoRecording, markVideoRecording, stopVideoRecording,
videoRecordingStatus and the videoRecordingEnded event: one tab recorded
to a fragmented H.264 MP4 at a constant frame rate, with an events
sidecar. The tab is captured through WebContentsVideoCaptureDevice at a
fixed size, letterboxed, as a hidden capture (KeepPageHidden,
SetStayHidden), so the window is never resized and the page sees nothing.
A sandboxed utility service, content/services/agent_video_encoding_service,
paces, encodes and muxes the frames and streams the file back, and the
browser writes it; content's Browser-domain handler holds the commands.
startVideoRecording's encoder names the H.264 encoder: auto (the GPU
process's, High profile, when it starts and passes a self-test, else
OpenH264, Baseline), hardware or software; the answer says which runs.
One encoder makes the whole file, written in fragments of about a second:
a failure after the start, a hardware encoder's included, ends the
recording with an error, and the file plays up to its last complete
fragment. The CDP cursor and its click mark are blended into the frames
by viz as a capture overlay, with or without --show-cdp-cursor, and each
press writes a click line to the sidecar; cursor: false leaves them out.
The system's own cursor is never in the file. The tab's sound is a
loopback of its audio group asked for directly from the audio service, so
the tab counts no capturer (agent_audio_capture), encoded in the service
as AAC or Opus (agent_audio_track). --mute-audio now zeroes the data in
services/audio's OutputController::OnMoreData, after the loopback
snoopers and before the power monitor's scan, instead of in
SyncReader::Read, so a recording of a muted browser has its sound while
the device plays silence and the tab still reads as silent. A recording
can move to another tab, and goes back when that tab closes while the one
it left is open; its time limit counts recorded time, not time paused;
videoRecordingStatus reports the browser's recording, whoever started it.

With redact, card number and security code fields and every element
marked with Page.agentMarkSecretField are painted, in the page itself
while the recording runs, as one black box each with no text or caret in
it; nothing is drawn differently while none runs. The client marks a
field before it puts the secret in (the answer is marked, gone, frame or
nothing), so the browser is never given a secret or a hash of one. Text
a page draws through a canvas is left as it is, and a secret a page
prints elsewhere is not hidden. The browser has viz require a redaction
generation, then tells every renderer
(content.mojom.Renderer.SetAgentRedaction); each renderer repaints and
stamps the compositor frames it painted after hearing of it (a
CompositorFrameMetadata field that cc carries), and viz shows black, in
any copy, a renderer frame without that stamp, so a part of a page that
has not repainted is black in the file; video and OffscreenCanvas frames
carry a stamp that lets them through. The marks are kept in the renderer
(core/paint/agent_redaction), never on the element, so a page cannot
tell a marked field from another, and a mark follows a secret that the
page's script passes on to the next editable element it focuses.
--agent-redaction-skip-renderers-for-testing, read in the browser process
only, tells no renderer, so a redacted recording is black throughout; it
can only make a recording blacker.

Riders: input-actions carries its lines in content/browser/BUILD.gn and
content's protocol_config.json; cursor-overlay those in
cdp_cursor_overlay.*; agent-snapshot those in page_handler.*, Page.pdl,
agent_snapshot_collector.mojom, agent_snapshot_collector_impl.*,
agent_card_fields.cc and Blink's inspector_protocol_config.json;
recording those in renderer.mojom, render_thread_impl.*, blink.h and
blink_initializer.cc; agent-fetch those in Browser.pdl. Its hooks in
render_process_host_impl.cc are this commit's own.
